{"assets":["/statement-assets/eea1e0b179e3a6b854b75967ed4c94d4350bfc7c7bc4fba8ca559be62208a66f.png","/statement-assets/b0d607c9dc8c21a7bd18275ec2b894ba68eeae6935d8246900e40f55d0f0f1fd.png","/statement-assets/df2e481d7f5621fa2a080f70bf8c3fa50efb9455b0c0f4697bfb8bc870fa012e.png","/statement-assets/5e957cdac6b1aaaf2ed3173e1599fcc58705e04620bae47f6ac9e0c0a925926d.png","/statement-assets/345ed2ecc71072d0a901671aaac4256ca7234cd4e226daff6888b96e4fc21db0.png","/statement-assets/f0247f180817e9bbeda0147b2a793f47e91a2f497ba1cbe8e80f18f12478a805.png","/statement-assets/c5e524f53daf42d6b1b8c1d6a1db66646052ab95cfe2dd60fdd23a75ec5ba270.png","/statement-assets/952d310a194bee7ef1ae680637324938e6296407764addc1b6e1b49c1ae08dc2.png","/statement-assets/71b232978a30a70ccf1b516d226d19144eeec5b914b9043a315bd346703c7e04.png","/statement-assets/06babe722a50d804ac051da695ea700f1dcccb0d9967d291735225d705ab0c23.png","/statement-assets/fd697ef0b927cdfb126569df141bcf5753be080a4ea0ed1042388800a1598869.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"935","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Fafa and Ancient Alphabet"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ancient Egyptians are known to have used a large set of symbols "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/eea1e0b179e3a6b854b75967ed4c94d4350bfc7c7bc4fba8ca559be62208a66f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" to write on the walls of the temples. Fafa and Fifa went to one of the temples and found two non-empty words "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S2"},{"kind":"text","text":" of equal lengths on the wall of temple written one below the other. Since this temple is very ancient, some symbols from the words were erased. The symbols in the set "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/eea1e0b179e3a6b854b75967ed4c94d4350bfc7c7bc4fba8ca559be62208a66f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" have equal probability for being in the position of any erased symbol."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fifa challenged Fafa to calculate the probability that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is lexicographically greater than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S2"},{"kind":"text","text":". Can you help Fafa with this task?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You know that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b0d607c9dc8c21a7bd18275ec2b894ba68eeae6935d8246900e40f55d0f0f1fd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", i. e. there were "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct characters in Egyptians' alphabet, in this problem these characters are denoted by integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" in alphabet order. A word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" is lexicographically greater than a word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the same length, if the words are same up to some position, and then the word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" has a larger character, than the word "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can prove that the probability equals to some fraction "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/df2e481d7f5621fa2a080f70bf8c3fa50efb9455b0c0f4697bfb8bc870fa012e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q"},{"kind":"text","text":" are coprime integers, and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5e957cdac6b1aaaf2ed3173e1599fcc58705e04620bae47f6ac9e0c0a925926d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Print as the answer the value "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/345ed2ecc71072d0a901671aaac4256ca7234cd4e226daff6888b96e4fc21db0.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", i. e. such a non-negative integer less than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/f0247f180817e9bbeda0147b2a793f47e91a2f497ba1cbe8e80f18f12478a805.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/c5e524f53daf42d6b1b8c1d6a1db66646052ab95cfe2dd60fdd23a75ec5ba270.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" means that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" give the same remainders when divided by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n,  m ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of each of the two words and the size of the alphabet "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/eea1e0b179e3a6b854b75967ed4c94d4350bfc7c7bc4fba8ca559be62208a66f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ ai ≤ m"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the symbols of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S1"},{"kind":"text","text":". If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the symbol at position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" was erased."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers representing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S2"},{"kind":"text","text":" with the same format as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the value "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/952d310a194bee7ef1ae680637324938e6296407764addc1b6e1b49c1ae08dc2.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"P"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Q"},{"kind":"text","text":" are coprime and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/df2e481d7f5621fa2a080f70bf8c3fa50efb9455b0c0f4697bfb8bc870fa012e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n0\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"500000004\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n1\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 26\n0 15 12 9 13 0 14\n11 1 0 13 15 12 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"230769233\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, the first word can be converted into ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":") or ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The second option is the only one that will make it lexicographically larger than the second word. So, the answer to the problem will be "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/71b232978a30a70ccf1b516d226d19144eeec5b914b9043a315bd346703c7e04.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", that is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"500000004"},{"kind":"text","text":", because "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/06babe722a50d804ac051da695ea700f1dcccb0d9967d291735225d705ab0c23.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there is no replacement for the zero in the second word that will make the first one lexicographically larger. So, the answer to the problem is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/fd697ef0b927cdfb126569df141bcf5753be080a4ea0ed1042388800a1598869.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", that is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"935D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/935/problem/D"}